# Normalise line endings on checkin, check out LF everywhere.
#
# Prophylactic in this phase, not remedial: nothing in the repo currently
# asserts on newline-bearing generated content. Measured before landing this —
# no snapshot matchers exist anywhere in the tree (no toMatchSnapshot,
# toMatchInlineSnapshot or toMatchFileSnapshot), and exactly one test reads a
# file from disk, which it writes itself into a temp dir. So no test today can
# go red on a CRLF checkout.
#
# It is landed anyway because the surviving POSIX MCP wrapper still emits
# newline-joined shell text, and Phase 7 will test it. A guard added after the
# first CRLF-sensitive assertion exists is a guard added one red Windows run
# too late.
* text=auto eol=lf
